Here's a JavaScript function `reorderAdjectives` that switches the order of adjectives in a sentence:

```javascript
function reorderAdjectives(sentence) {
  // Split the sentence into an array of words
  const words = sentence.split(' ');

  // Filter out common stop words (you can customize this list)
  const stopWords = ['a', 'an', 'the'];
  const filteredWords = words.filter((word) => !stopWords.includes(word.toLowerCase()));

  // Find all adjectives in the filtered words
  const adjectives = filteredWords.filter((word) => /\b[a-zA-Z]{1,2}[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+\b/g.test(word));

  // Reverse the order of adjectives
  const reversedAdjectives = adjectives.reverse();

  // Concatenate the filtered and reversed adjectives with the original sentence
  const result = filteredWords.concat(reversedAdjectives).concat(words.slice(words.indexOf('be') + 1)).join(' ');

  return result;
}
```

